# <<TOPIC>>.harness

<<TOPIC_BLURB>>

This is a *reference / discussion harness* — it bundles the literature library (`.knowledge/`), project notes, and the Zulip bridge to the `<<ZULIP_STREAM>>` stream on `zulip.hkust-gz.edu.cn`. Implementation code lives elsewhere.

## Getting started

### 1. Install the `zlp-harness` plugin

The skills for onboarding, downloading references, and replying on Zulip are provided by the `zlp-harness` plugin. Install it once per machine — add this to your `~/.claude/settings.json`:

```jsonc
"extraKnownMarketplaces": {
  "zlp-harness": {
    "source": { "source": "github", "repo": "CodingThrust/zlp-harness" }
  }
},
"enabledPlugins": {
  "zlp-harness@zlp-harness": true
}
```

### 2. Clone and onboard

Open [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code) in any directory and paste:

```
clone https://github.com/<<GITHUB_REMOTE>> and invoke the onboard skill.
```

The `onboard` skill detects what you already have, walks you through getting a hkust-gz Zulip API key, sets up the workspace, and verifies the bridge with `make zulip-whoami`.

For everything else (commands, knowledge base layout, adding references, posting to Zulip), see [`CLAUDE.md`](CLAUDE.md).
